<body><table class="page" id="page"><tr style="height:1px"><td><table class="header"><tr><td class="logocell"><a href="/" title="EasyChair home page"><img class="leftlogo" src="/images/logoEC_short.png"/></a></td><td class="rolecell">EasyChair Smart CFP</td><td style="width: 99%"></td><td class="helplink"><a class="toplinks" href="/docs/home" title="User guide">User guide</a></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr style="height:99%"><td class="menu_and_content"><div class="menu" id="menu0"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="menu" style="position:static; visibility:visible"><tr><td class="top" id="menu1" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu1','/cfp',{&quot;a&quot;:null})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu1')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu1')" title="Main page">Home</td><td class="top" id="menu2" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu2','/cfp/choose',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu2')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu2')" title="Create a new CFP">New CFP</td><td class="top" id="menu3" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu3','/cfp/all',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu3')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu3')" title="Manage my CFPs">My CFPs</td><td class="top" id="menu4" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu4','/cfp/watchlist',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu4')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu4')" title="My CFP watchlist">Watchlist</td></tr></table></div><div class="search_row" id="cfp:search:row"><form action="/cfp/search" id="search-form"><input id="search-input" name="query" placeholder="Search" type="text"/></form></div><div class="summary"><div class="pagetitle">CFP</div></div><div class="content" id="content"><div class="subcontent"><div id="cfp" style="clear:right"><table class="title_table"><tr><td class="single"><div id="cfptitle">TrustSecAI 2027: 1st International Workshop on AI Security &amp; Trustworthy Autonomous Cybersecurity</div><div id="cfpvenue">Delft, the Netherlands</div><div id="cfpdateplace">Delft, Netherlands, April 13-15, 2027</div></td></tr></table><table class="date_table"><tr><td>Conference web page</td><td><a href="https://rayentech.github.io/TrustSecAI2027/" target="_blank">https://rayentech.github.io/TrustSecAI2027/</a></td></tr><tr><td>Submission link</td><td><a href="https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=trustsecai2027" target="_blank">https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=trustsecai2027</a></td></tr><tr><td>Abstract registration deadline</td><td>November 20, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Submission deadline</td><td>November 27, 2026</td></tr></table><div class="topics">Topics: <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=17645221" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_green bg_gray1">artificial intelligence security</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=24512651" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_black bg_cobalt">trustworthy and responsible ai</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=44330005" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_navy bg_seagreenlight">autonomous and ai driven cybersecurity</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=44330007" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_blue bg_fuchsia">cybersecurity and threat intelligence</span></a></div><h2>TrustSecAI 2027</h2><p><strong>TrustSecAI 2027 - </strong>1st International Workshop on AI Security &amp; Trustworthy Autonomous Cybersecurity</p><p><u><em><strong>Notice : The full workshop title must be included at the top of the paper submission.</strong></em></u></p><p><strong>About TrustSecAI 2027</strong></p><p>TrustSecAI 2027 is an international research workshop dedicated to advancing the security, trustworthiness, and resilience of artificial intelligence systems and autonomous cybersecurity technologies. The workshop aims to bring together researchers, academics, industry professionals, and practitioners to exchange ideas, present original research, and discuss emerging challenges at the intersection of AI security, trustworthy AI, and cybersecurity.</p><p>As AI systems become increasingly integrated into critical applications and cybersecurity operations, ensuring their robustness, reliability, transparency, and resistance to malicious manipulation is essential. TrustSecAI 2027 seeks to foster scientific discussion and collaboration on innovative approaches to securing AI-enabled systems and developing trustworthy, intelligent, and autonomous cyber defense capabilities.</p><p>The workshop welcomes contributions addressing theoretical foundations, novel methodologies, practical implementations, experimental evaluations, and emerging research directions.</p><p><strong>Topics of Interest</strong></p><p>Topics of interest include, but are not limited to:</p><p>Artificial Intelligence Security: Adversarial machine learning, attacks against AI models, data poisoning, model extraction, and AI-specific vulnerabilities.</p><p>Trustworthy and Responsible AI: Robustness, explainability, transparency, accountability, reliability, and AI assurance.</p><p>Cybersecurity and Threat Intelligence: Intrusion detection, threat analysis, vulnerability assessment, malware analysis, and intelligent cyber defense.</p><p>Autonomous and AI-Driven Cybersecurity: Autonomous security systems, AI-assisted security operations, automated incident response, intelligent threat hunting, and adaptive cyber defense.</p><p>Secure AI Engineering: Security-by-design, AI system testing, risk assessment, secure deployment, and continuous security monitoring.</p><p>Privacy-Preserving and Secure Machine Learning: Federated learning security, privacy-enhancing technologies, and protection of sensitive data.</p><p>AI for Emerging Digital Infrastructures: Security of intelligent networks, cloud and edge computing, IoT, and next-generation communication systems.</p><p><strong>Submission Guidelines</strong></p><p>TrustSecAI 2027 invites researchers and practitioners to submit original contributions relevant to the workshop's scope.</p><p>All submissions must present original work that is not simultaneously submitted to another journal or conference. Papers should clearly describe their research contributions, methodology, evaluation, and relevance to the workshop themes.</p><p>Potential submission categories include:</p><p>Full research papers: Original theoretical or applied research presenting novel methods, technical contributions, experimental results, or comprehensive evaluations.</p><p>Short papers: Preliminary research results, emerging ideas, novel approaches, or focused technical contributions.</p><p>Posters and work-in-progress contributions: Early-stage research, innovative concepts, and ongoing projects that would benefit from discussion and feedback, subject to the workshop's submission policy.</p><p>Submission platform: The official submission link will be announced once the submission system is configured.</p><p>Authors should follow the submission format, page limits, review policy, and deadlines specified in the official workshop and conference instructions. Acceptance and publication arrangements will be communicated by the organizers.</p><p><strong>Committees</strong></p><p><strong>Program Committee (TPC)</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Rayen Gaied</strong> (Tunisia Polytechnic School, Tunisia; European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI) Ambassador)</p></li><li><p><strong>Dr. Sofien Mhatli</strong> (Tunisia Polytechnic School, Tunisia)</p></li><li><p><strong>Mihaela Curca</strong> (The Romanian National Cyber Security Directorate, Romania; European Commission, European Union)</p></li><li><p><strong>Lorenzo Mucchi</strong> (University of Florence, Italy)</p></li><li><p><strong>Alice Piemonti</strong> (Martel Innovate, Switzerland)</p></li><li><p><strong>Bruno Banelli</strong> (European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI), France)</p></li><li><p><strong>Marcos Altarriba Roig</strong> (Universitat Politècnica de València (UPV), Spain)</p></li></ul><p><strong>Organizing Committee</strong></p><p>The Organizing Committee will coordinate the workshop's scientific program, communications, logistics, and collaboration with the main conference organizers.</p><p><strong>Important Dates</strong></p><p>Submission deadlines, notification of acceptance, camera-ready deadlines, and the workshop date will be announced once confirmed by the organizers.</p><p><strong>Contact</strong></p><p>All questions about submissions should be emailed to rayen.gaied.engineer@outlook.com or sofienmhatli2017@gmail.com</p><p>We welcome contributions from the international research community and look forward to encouraging meaningful discussions and collaboration on AI security, trustworthy AI, and autonomous cybersecurity.</p></div></div></div></td></tr><tr><td class="footer">Copyright © 2002 – 2026 EasyChair</td></tr></table></body></html>
